acvd (4.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial Debian packaging, ported from the neurofedora acvd.spec (4.0-5).
  * Library-only build against system VTK (examples install generically named
    binaries such as viewer and icp, and nothing downstream needs them).
  * 0001-install-the-install-tree-ACVDConfig.patch: upstream generates a
    correct install-tree ACVDConfig.cmake under CMakeFiles/ but install()s the
    build-tree one, so consumers of find_package(ACVD) got include directories
    pointing at the builder's source checkout. MITK's Remeshing module failed
    with "vtkIsotropicDiscreteRemeshing.h: No such file or directory".
  * 0002-qualify-std-iostream-in-public-headers.patch: the header-only
    DiscreteRemeshing templates use unqualified cout/cerr/endl without
    <iostream>. Template bodies are only diagnosed on instantiation, so this
    surfaces in consumers, not in ACVD's own build (MITK: 35 errors). Qualify
    with std:: rather than leaking a using-directive into every consumer.
  * 0003-drop-header-only-DiscreteRemeshing-from-ACVD_LIBRARIES.patch:
    ACVD_LIBRARIES listed vtkDiscreteRemeshing, which is header-only and has
    no library, so linking ${ACVD_LIBRARIES} failed with "cannot find
    -lvtkDiscreteRemeshing".
  * Force-include an <iostream> prelude for ACVD's own .cxx sources, which
    have the same problem but are not shipped.

 -- Morgan Hough <morgan.hough@gmail.com>  Wed, 23 Sep 2026 10:01:12 -0700
